350
00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:55.860
You're like, but I would think, lady, how do you hear your alarm?
你来了一句：不过我在想，女士，你怎么能听见闹钟响呢？

351
00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:57.040
I hear it.
我听到了。

352
00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.400
You hear it through the earplugs and the noise and all the things.
你透过耳塞、噪音以及各种声音听到了它。

353
00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:00.780
Yeah.
对。

354
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:01.460
Okay.
好的。

355
00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:02.320
Well.
好吧。

356
00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.540
Well, you didn't that morning.
好吧，那天早上你可没听到。

357
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:04.940
I guess not.
我想也是吧。

358
00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.560
Lily, I love that question.
莉莉，我太喜欢那个问题了。

359
00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:10.480
I love these little slice of life shares.
我喜欢这些生活小片段的分享。

360
00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.700
I think they're so fun.
我觉得它们太有趣了。

361
00:12:11.860 --> 00:12:14.180
I love our new format for Office Ladies.
我喜欢我们《办公室女士》的新形式。

362
00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:20.500
I was thinking about it and just how much I love it because of how much it involves getting to hear from people.
我在想这件事，以及我有多喜欢它，因为这能让我们听到很多人的声音。

363
00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:21.060
Yes.
没错。

364
00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:25.760
It's sort of a callback to the very beginning of Office Ladies where people would call in and read the summary.
这有点像《办公室女士》最初的致敬，当时大家会打电话进来朗读剧情摘要。

365
00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:26.240
Remember?
还记得吗？

366
00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:26.960
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

367
00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.120
And we loved that.
我们当时很喜欢那样。

368
00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:28.640
We did.
确实如此。

369
00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:29.720
So here we are.
所以我们就这样开始了。

370
00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.560
Well, listen, we're going to take a break and then we are going to get into Boom Roasted.
听着，我们要休息一下，然后就要进入“痛贬”环节了。

371
00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:45.470
We are back.
我们回来了。

372
00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:54.410
And before we dig into all of the additional roasting from this episode, I want us to remember Michael's expectations for this roaSt.
在我们深入探讨本集的所有额外痛贬之前，我想让我们回想一下迈克尔对这次痛贬的期望。

373
00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:54.770
Yeah.
对。

374
00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.370
Because he has a lot of expectations for how the roast is going to go.
因为他对痛贬会如何进行有着很高的期望。

375
00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:04.490
In re-watching this episode, I was so excited to find that there was an extended scene between Michael and Daryl.
在重看这一集时，我很高兴地发现迈克尔和达里尔之间有一段加长场景。

376
00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:09.090
You might remember before the roast, he goes down to the warehouse to talk to Daryl.
你可能记得在痛贬开始前，他下到仓库去找达里尔谈话。

377
00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:12.250
He wants to talk about what is the stage going to look like?
他想谈谈舞台会是什么样子的？

378
00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.050
What kind of chair is he going to have?
他会坐什么样的椅子？

379
00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.890
It's this amazing scene and it was all expanded for the super fan.
这是一个绝妙的场景，而且全部都是为超级粉丝版扩展的。

380
00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.590
I think we need to hear it.
我觉得我们需要听听看。

381
00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.250
So that's the stage.
所以这就是舞台。

382
00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:22.010
Yes.
是的。

383
00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:22.970
All right.
好吧。

384
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:23.290
Yeah.
对。

385
00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:24.190
You know what?
你知道吗？

386
00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:24.610
That'll work.
这样就行。

387
00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:25.690
That'll work for my roaSt.
这适合我的痛贬。

388
00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.650
Supposed to be working as a warehouse.
这本该是个仓库。

389
00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:30.090
Well, this is all about morale, Daryl.
好吧，这全关乎士气，达里尔。

390
00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:37.430
I will need a big chair, a comfy chair, like a throne for the man of honor.
我需要一把大椅子，一把舒服的椅子，就像为荣誉嘉宾准备的宝座一样。

391
00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:42.210
And I think all the other roasters should be up here on stage as well.
而且我认为所有其他参与痛贬的人也应该在台上面对观众。

392
00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.310
Everyone's on the stage?
所有人都上台？

393
00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:44.710
Yeah, like a Comedy Central roaSt.
对，就像喜剧中心的痛贬节目一样。

394
00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:45.530
Who's in the audience?
谁在观众席里？

395
00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:47.270
The audience will be in the audience.
观众当然在观众席里。

396
00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.590
We'll charge $10 a head.
我们每人收十美元。

397
00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:49.450
Charge who?
收谁的钱？

398
00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.250
We'll need alcohol, because that's very important for a roaSt.
我们需要酒精，因为这对于痛贬来说非常重要。

399
00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.850
You need to get people drunk.
你需要把人们灌醉。

400
00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.430
And you need something to spit.
而且你需要点用来吐的东西。

401
00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.030
Ah, boo!
啊，嘘！

402
00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:58.810
You going to be spitting in here?
你待会儿要在这儿喷口水吗？

403
00:13:58.870 --> 00:13:59.630
Spit takes, yes.
喷水梗，对的。

404
00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:00.730
I'll be doing some spit takes.
我会做一些喷水梗。

405
00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:01.930
If it's funny enough.
如果够好笑的话。

406
00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.370
Or I will do finger guns.
或者我会做手枪手势。

407
00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:08.100
Or, right?
或者，对吧？

408
00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:08.860
Sammy Davis Jr.
小萨米·戴维斯。

409
00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:09.200
move.
走开。

410
00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:09.880
But you know that.
不过你懂的。

411
00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.420
Or I will double over.
或者我会笑得直不起腰。

412
00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.620
Or I will do the point.
或者我会指着。

413
00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.560
Like, oh, you got me.
比如，哦，你把我难倒了。

414
00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:15.860
What?
什么？

415
00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.120
I got your big picture you wanted.
我拿到了你想要的大幅照片。

416
00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:17.880
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

417
00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:18.900
I need a big picture.
我需要一张大幅照片。

418
00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.660
Something to cover the whole back of the dais.
能盖住主席台整个背板的东西。

419
00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:21.520
I have to go to the printer.
我得去一趟印刷厂。

420
00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:22.480
Well, go, please.
行，快去吧，求你了。

421
00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.660
Oh, and get me a drum and a cymbal.
哦，顺便帮我带个大军鼓和镲。

422
00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:25.760
I want to do ba-dum-buMs.
我想来个咚咚锵。

423
00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:26.340
Rim shots.
边击。

424
00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:27.580
No, ba-dum-buMs.
不，是咚咚锵。

425
00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:28.800
Technical term is rim shots.
专业术语叫边击。

426
00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.800
By the way, when I was watching the roast, he does all those things.
话说回来，我刚才看吐槽大会的时候，他把那些动作全做了。

427
00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:40.160
He does, obviously, the ba-dum-bums, but he does finger guns.
他显然做了咚咚锵，但他还做了手枪手势。

428
00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:41.080
He does them all.
他全做了。

429
00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:41.440
He does the point.
他还做了那个指的手势。

430
00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:42.660
It's amazing.
太绝了。

431
00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:49.000
I am really realizing, though, that ba-dum-bums, ba-dum-bums is something I'd probably say.
不过我突然意识到，咚咚锵，咚咚锵这种词我平时可能也会说。

432
00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:53.160
It's making me think of, like, when we first started re-watching The Office, when I would
这让我想到，比如我们刚开始重温《办公室》时，我把那种隔着百叶窗拍镜头的

433
00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.380
call the shot through the blinds the peep shot.
叫作偷窥镜。

434
00:14:55.640 --> 00:14:56.280
The peep shot.
偷窥镜。

435
00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.120
And you're like, you mean the spy shot.
然后你说，你是说偷拍镜。

436
00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:01.140
Well, it's just that we called it a spy shot.
好吧，只是我们管它叫偷拍镜。

437
00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:01.900
I know.
我知道。

438
00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.300
It's what I think the true term, not the peep shot.
我觉得那才是真正的词，而不是偷窥镜。

439
00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:09.740
All right, you guys, now it's time to dive into the candy bag alts.
好了，各位，现在我们要来深入聊聊“糖果袋”备选片段了。

440
00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:10.760
Oh, it's so good.
哦，太棒了。

441
00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.900
We thought we would start right before the roast begins with some talking heads that really
我们打算在吐槽大会开始前，先播放一些访谈，它们真正

442
00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:20.640
set the tone for how people in the office felt about the roast and how hard they were
奠定了基调，展现了办公室里的人对这场吐槽的看法，以及他们打算

443
00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.480
going to go at Michael.
对迈克尔下多狠的手。

444
00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.820
I'm going to kick us off with a candy bag alt for Angela Martin.
我先来分享一个安吉拉·马丁的“糖果袋”备选片段。

445
00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.160
Angela would have said,
安吉拉当时会说，

446
00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:30.440
I wish I'd thought of writing down every problem I have with Michael for the last five
我要是早想到把过去五年里我对迈克尔的所有意见都写下来

447
00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:30.860
years.
就好了。

448
00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.260
Angela pretends to find a notebook, which she holds up.
安吉拉假装找到一个笔记本，把它高高举起。

449
00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.120
Oh, wait a minute.
哦，等等。

450
00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:37.980
And she points to it.
然后她指了指那个本子。

451
00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:42.900
She has been keeping a journal of every time Michael has pissed her off.
她一直记着迈克尔每次惹毛她的日记。

452
00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.320
That's pretty amazing.
这可真够厉害的。

453
00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.980
Well, Andy had some real gems, too.
安迪也有一些绝妙的发言。

454
00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.760
Here is one of his talking heads.
这是他的其中一段单人访谈。

455
00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.480
Andy was going to say,
安迪本来打算说：

456
00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.680
every now and then, you got to just take the gloves off and really rip into someone.
偶尔你就是得脱下手套，狠狠地把某人痛骂一顿。

457
00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.260
For the Bernards, that's traditionally been on Thanksgiving.
对伯纳德家来说，传统上这都是在感恩节进行的。

458
00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:03.720
So this will be a nice test run.
所以这将是一次很好的彩排。

459
00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.580
Can you imagine Thanksgiving at Andy Bernard's parents' house?
你能想象在安迪·伯纳德父母家过感恩节吗？

460
00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:08.240
I cannot.
我想象不出来。

461
00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.380
How many jabs they throw at him?
他们会对他冷嘲热讽多少次？

462
00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.440
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

463
00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:12.260
All right.
好吧。

464
00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.400
Here's one from Kevin.
这是凯文的一段。

465
00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:14.600
Kevin would have said,
凯文原本会说：

466
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:20.160
Michael letting us tell him how much he sucks is probably the coolest thing he's ever done.
迈克尔让我们告诉他他有多烂，这可能是他做过最酷的事了。

467
00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:23.420
He set up a PA system in everything.
他还到处架设了扩音系统。

468
00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:28.280
And lastly, here is one from Oscar that really paints a picture.
最后，这是奥斯卡的一段，非常生动形象。

469
00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:31.040
I mean, Michael has no idea what he's in for.
我是说，迈克尔根本不知道他将要面对什么。

470
00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:32.760
Oscar would have said,
奥斯卡本来会说：

471
00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:38.980
As an accountant, it's my duty to measure the value of roasting Michael against the potential of getting fired.
作为一名会计，我有责任权衡狠狠吐槽迈克尔的价值与被解雇的风险。

472
00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:42.500
But as a man, I have no choice but to destroy him.
但作为一个男人，我别无选择，只能摧毁他。

473
00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.080
Destroy him.
摧毁他。

474
00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:44.540
Destroy.
摧毁。

475
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:45.260
Oh.
噢。

476
00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.660
And if you think the roasts that made it into the actual episode were rough on Michael,
如果你觉得正片里那些吐槽对迈克尔来说已经够狠了，

477
00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.640
just wait until you hear the alts.
那你就等着听听备选片段吧。

478
00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:52.320
OMG.
我的天哪。

479
00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.940
But guys, it's time for the roaSt.
但是各位，吐槽大会要开始了。

480
00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.160
Michael is so excited to get it started.
迈克尔兴奋得迫不及待地想开始了。

481
00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.460
This is going to take a turn very quickly.
接下来局势很快就会急转直下。

482
00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.840
But let's hear his opening speech just full of enthusiasm.
但让我们先听听他那充满热情的开场白。

483
00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.200
Woo!
呜！

484
00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:07.020
Welcome, welcome, welcome, welcome, welcome.
欢迎，欢迎，欢迎，欢迎，欢迎。

485
00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.460
You are all jerks.
你们全都是混蛋。

486
00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:10.740
Just kidding.
开玩笑的。

487
00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:11.820
Not yet, anyway.
至少现在还不是。

488
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:15.380
Welcome to the roast of Mr. Michael Scott.
欢迎来到迈克尔·斯科特先生的吐槽大会。

489
00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:19.020
If you're here for the Grabowski wedding, it is the second door on the left.
如果您是来参加格拉博夫斯基的婚礼的，请走左边的第二扇门。

490
00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.720
So we all know how these work.
所以我们都知道这流程怎么走。

491
00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:23.880
Needs to get crazy.
得疯狂起来。

492
00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.100
Take your best shot.
尽情放马过来吧。

493
00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:32.600
But I am going to sit right off a chair, and whoever wants to come up and roast me, you may.
但我会坐在椅子旁边，谁想上来吐槽我，请便。

494
00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:33.160
Okay.
好的。

495
00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.040
Well, Angela, you are first up.
安吉拉，你是第一个。

496
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:36.500
Oh, yeah.
哦，耶。

497
00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:37.740
I charge the stage.
我冲向舞台。

498
00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:38.160
Yes.
没错。

499
00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:41.940
And dare I say, I think it's the best roaSt.
我敢说，我认为这是最棒的吐槽。

500
00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:42.480
No.
才不呢。

501
00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:43.440
I really do.
我是认真的。

502
00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:44.960
I really, really do.
我是真的、真的很认真。

503
00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:46.580
And I didn't see it coming.
而且我完全没料到会这样。

504
00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:53.800
You know, like, I think as a fan of the show, you don't necessarily think that Angela is going to be a really good roaster.
你知道的，作为这部剧的粉丝，你可能不会觉得安吉拉会是一个很厉害的脱口秀吐槽者。

505
00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:54.680
But she is.
但她确实是。

506
00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.880
She's going to roast him, like, a la Jeff Foxworthy style.
她要吐槽他，就像杰夫·福克斯沃西的风格那样。

507
00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.500
That's how it's described in the script.
剧本里就是这么写的。

508
00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:05.100
It says, Angela does a very bland Jeff Foxworthy.
上面写着，安吉拉进行了一次非常平淡无奇的杰夫式吐槽。

509
00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:12.680
And something I feel like we should share with people is that the superfan episode does not have a bunch of extra roast stuff in it.
我觉得有件事我们应该告诉大家，那就是超级粉丝版里并没有包含一大堆额外的吐槽内容。

510
00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:13.440
That's right.
没错。

511
